{# Closest in meaning — neighbours derived from the semantic search vectors.

   This is a different signal from the topic tags. Topics are editorial: what
   I decided a post was filed under. These are computed from the embeddings
   already generated for search, so they reflect what the writing is actually
   about, and they surface pairings across sections that no shared tag links.

   Renders nothing when a post has no neighbour above the similarity floor.
   Roughly a third of entries are singular enough that they don't, which is
   the honest outcome rather than a padded list. That share went UP when the
   chrome leak was fixed: a lot of the old "similarity" was entries sharing
   navigation boilerplate rather than sharing a subject.

   Data: src/site/_data/related.json, written by scripts/compute-related.mjs. #}
{%- set near = related[page.url] -%}
{%- if near and near.length -%}
<div class="kh-section-head kh-u-margin__top--1200" data-pagefind-ignore>
  <h2 class="kh-text-heading--2">Closest in meaning</h2>
  <span class="kh-meta">By similarity, not by tag</span>
</div>
<ol class="kh-near" data-pagefind-ignore>
  {%- for n in near %}
  <li class="kh-near__item">
    <a class="kh-near__link" href="{{ n.url | url }}">{{ n.title | safe }}</a>
    {#- The score is stated rather than drawn. It is a soft signal on an
        unfamiliar scale, so a bar would imply more precision than it has. -#}
    <span class="kh-near__score" title="Cosine similarity of the entries' embeddings">{{ n.score }}</span>
  </li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ol>
{%- endif -%}
